<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 19.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 19.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for June 19, in U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states:</p>
<p>		ASW	     AH	   PH 13 PCT    PH 14  PCT</p>
<p>    Jun    181.00 -3.0  189.50 -3.0  194.00 -2.0  205.00 -1.5</p>
<p>    Jul    178.00 -3.0  186.50 -3.0  191.00 -2.0  204.00 -1.5</p>
<p>    Aug    173.50 -3.0  183.00 -3.0  187.50 -2.0  202.00 -1.5</p>
<p>    Sept   175.50 -1.0  185.00 -1.0  188.50 -1.0  202.00 -1.5</p>
<p>    Oct    177.50 -1.0  186.00 -1.0  189.50 -1.0  203.00 -1.5</p>
<p>    Nov    178.50 -1.0  187.00 -1.0  190.50 -1.0  204.00 -1.5</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased by A$2.50 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	172.50</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  147.50	    Port Adelaide	 149.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     147.75	    Port Giles	    149.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	145.50	    Wallaroo		147.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    144.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     147.50	    Port Lincoln	  150.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   148.00	    Thevenard	     145.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 147.00	     Esperance	    152.25</p>
<p>    Portland	148.00	     Albany		 153.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    155.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    153.25</p>
<p>AWB MARKET COMMENTARY: Another weaker day. This market needs a major weather scare or some world demand to appear to fuel some kind of strength.</p>
<p>AWB cash bids for New South Wales A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>			 1996/97 crop		1997/98 crop</p>
<p>    ASW/APW	  A$174.00 Newcastle	A$162.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    AH1:	     A$184.00 Newcastle	A$175.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    PH 13:	   A$209.00 Newcastle	A$190.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    Feed Barley    A$147.50 *State avge    A$125.00 *State avge</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	ex farm Nov/Dec</p>
<p>    Sorghum	  A$156.00 Newcastle	No bid</p>
<p>    Triticale	A$159.00 *State avge     A$119.00 *ex farm</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	 Dec/Jan</p>
<p>NOTES: The multigrade indicator price represents the AWB's view of the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered by the AWB.</p>
<p>ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; PW = Premium White; Percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>* Prices vary between regions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
